hydrocal for Windows
 ====================

 Version @HYDROCAL_VERSION@, revision @HYDROCAL_REVISION@ (@HYDROCAL_GITID@)
 Built @HYDROCAL_REVISION_DATE@

 Contents
 --------
   hydrocal_win.exe   prebuilt 64-bit console program (OpenMP enabled)
   hydrocal.sln       Visual Studio 2022 solution
   hydrocal.vcxproj   Visual Studio C++ project (x64 and Win32, Debug/Release)
   ReadMe.txt         this file
   buildinfo.h        version header generated at build time

 Running
 -------
 Run hydrocal_win.exe from a command line.  It reads a hydrocal input file
 (see doc/examples in the source repository) and reports

   ###  hydrocal revision     : @HYDROCAL_REVISION@

 so you can confirm which build you are running.

 No installation and no extra DLLs are needed; the executable is statically
 linked.

 Building with Visual Studio
 --------------------------
 The project files are a convenience for people who prefer MSVC to mingw.
 They are generated from the same source list as the CMake build, so they
 always match the sources of this release.  They do NOT ship the sources:
 extract this zip into the root of a hydrocal source checkout (the directory
 that contains src\ and CMakeLists.txt) and open hydrocal.sln.

 Visual Studio 2022 or newer with the "Desktop development with C++" workload
 is required.  For OpenMP support on MSVC, the v2.0 runtime is used
 automatically; omit <OpenMPSupport> from the project if it is unavailable.

 Building with CMake and mingw-w64 instead
 ----------------------------------------
 From the source root:

   cmake -B build-win -S . \
         -DCMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE=cmake/toolchain-mingw-x86_64.cmake \
         -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
   cmake --build build-win

 Optional dependencies (Boost, FLINT) are not available for the mingw target,
 so the corresponding hydrocal features fall back to the portable
 implementations.  For full functionality build on Linux or with MSVC.

 Please report problems at https://github.com/sschippe/hydrocal/issues